.TH DUI 8 2026-11-03 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
dui \- install or update DarqOS from a distribution tarball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dui
.RB [ \-\-boot ]
.RI [ tarball ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dui
(DarqOS Updater/Installer) installs DarqOS from a distribution tarball
made by
.BR mkdist :
the
.I tarball
given, or the latest, downloaded.
It is used both for the first install on a host and for later
updates.
It must be run as root.
.PP
.B dui
performs these steps, stopping with an error if any fails:
.IP 1. 4
Without a
.IR tarball ,
download
.B $DIST_BASE/$DIST_FILE
into
.I /tmp
with
.BR wget (1).
.IP 2.
Remove any existing
.BR $DIST ,
and unpack the tarball into it, owned by root.
.IP 3.
Run
.BR $DIST/darq/bin/install ,
passing it
.BR \-\-boot .
.IP 4.
Remove
.BR $DIST .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-boot
Make DarqOS the machine's default boot: see
.BR install (8).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARQ
Installation root.
Default:
.IR /darq .
.TP
.B DIST
Staging directory for the unpacked distribution.
Default:
.BR $DARQ/dist .
.TP
.B DIST_FILE
Name of the tarball to download.
Default:
.IR darqos-latest.tar.gz .
.TP
.B DIST_BASE
URL of the directory to download it from.
Default:
.IR https://www.0x1.org/d/darq .
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /tmp/ DIST_FILE
The downloaded tarball.
It is not removed afterwards.
.TP
.I $DIST/darq/bin/install
The install script run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if it installed; 1 if a step, or the install, failed; 2 for a bad
option.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Progress is written to standard output as lines starting
.RB \(lq Ok: \(rq,
and errors to standard error as lines starting
.RB \(lq Error: \(rq.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install (8),
.BR wget (1)
